      "**Tribal Communities in Border Areas:** Communities living in remote border areas (e.g., along the India-Burma border) whose territories fell within India's defined territory became citizens automatically if domiciled there.",
      "**Persons in Transit During Partition:** Individuals who were temporarily in Pakistan at the time of Partition but had their permanent home in India and returned — their domiciliary intent was key to Article 5 citizenship.",
